; Move a bitmap address down one pixel row
;
; Steps the address of a screen bitmap byte down by one pixel row, following the Spectrum screen layout: INC H inside
; a character cell; after the eighth line it moves to the first line of the next character row (L+32) and, on a carry,
; into the next third of the screen. Used by the character printer (#R$9EE4) and the bitmap fill #R$9F94.
; .
; Hardware: knows the layout of the screen bitmap at $4000-$57FF.
;
; HL Address of a byte in the screen bitmap
; O:HL Address of the byte one pixel row below
@label=NextPixelRow
c$9F17 INC H         ;
 $9F18 LD A,H        ;
 $9F19 AND $07       ;
 $9F1B RET NZ        ;
 $9F1C LD A,L        ;
@isub=ADD A,SCREEN_COLS
 $9F1D ADD A,$20     ; next character row
 $9F1F LD L,A        ;
 $9F20 RET C         ;
 $9F21 LD A,H        ;
@isub=SUB THIRD_STEP
 $9F22 SUB $08       ;
 $9F24 LD H,A        ;
 $9F25 RET           ;
